# desc: [blocked 2026-10-27] DFlash2 draft instead of the MTP head — the draft loads but vLLM 0.32's Qwen4Exp guard admits only MTP/ngram drafters (vllm#56088; public patch recipe: PixelML/deepspec-qwen38-flash-next). Fallback: ./flash serve default
#
# Status (boot on the GB10, 2026-10-27): method=dflash parses, the snapshot resolution and
# YaRN max_model_len work, and vLLM resolves DFlash2DraftModel - then the engine's
# Qwen4Exp verify_and_update_config raises "supports only its native MTP checkpoint and
# linear n-gram proposers" (vllm/model_executor/models/config.py). Not a draft-repo problem:
# five engine-side blockers are catalogued with patches at
# https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/56088 and
# https://github.com/PixelML/deepspec-qwen38-flash-next/tree/main/serving
# (measured there on 2x GB10 TP2 with a different drafter, eager mode, 8k context).
# Keep this profile to re-test once the allowlist + aux hidden-state capture land upstream.
MODE=hybrid
YARN=1
CTX=500000
MTP=0
DRAFT_MODEL=incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2
DRAFT_TOKENS=7
# DFlash2 needs the target's FULL vocabulary (the speculators docs reject pruned draft
# vocabularies), so the MTP-head draft-vocab prune (which defaults to on) is disabled here.
# It only ever applied to the MTP head anyway; set explicitly so the serve line reads truthfully.
DRAFT_VOCAB=0
